03578186],"scale":[1,0.9999999403953552,1.0000001192092896],"translation":[-9.484210750088096e-09,0.40733101963996887,-2.0954757928848267e-09]},{"children":[48],"name":"calf_r","rotation":[0.058844517916440964,-0.2321772277355194,0.008530084043741226,0.9708544611930847],"scale":[0.9999998807907104,0.9999997615814209,0.9999999403953552],"translation":[-5.587935447692871e-09,0.39470696449279785,7.450580596923828e-09]},{"children":[49],"name":"thigh_r","rotation":[-0.958074688911438,0.09174000471830368,-0.2139034867286682,0.16709880530834198],"scale":[0.9999998211860657,0.9999999403953552,0.9999985098838806],"translation":[-0.10147152096033096,-0.003829043358564377,-0.010990308597683907]},{"children":[42,46,50],"name":"pelvis","rotation":[0.5305899977684021,-1.5553862193127784e-16,-3.88809262563683e-10,0.8476285934448242],"translation":[0,-0.013216575607657433,0.8744488954544067]},{"children":[51],"name":"Root","rotation":[-0.7071067690849304,0,0,0.7071067690849304],"translation":[0,-0.0005625183694064617,6.100162863731384e-08]},{"mesh":0,"name":"Body","skin":0},{"mesh":1,"name":"Eyebrows","skin":0},{"mesh":2,"name":"Eyelashes","skin":0},{"mesh":3,"name":"Eyes","skin":0},{"mesh":4,"name":"Teeth","skin":0},{"mesh":5,"name":"Tongue","skin":0},{"children":[53,54,55,56,57,58,52,60,61,62,63],"name":"Ellen Baran","extras":{"persona":{"residentId":"AH-R0170","personId":"AH-R0170","name":"Ellen Baran","age":44,"occupation":"Rail maintenance worker","home":"the neighborhood around Market Flats","episode":"Five missing lunches","biography":"stories/residents/02/02-five-missing-lunches.md#ah-r0170","life":"“I left machine work for the railroad when the cold started to hurt my fingers.” People around the corner by Juniper Tailor know Ellen by a small Friday habit. Ellen looks at the things people actually bring in for repair before looking in the display window.","voice":"I store nuts in my tin. Finding somebody else's lunch inside made me remember to eat.","appearance":"On an ordinary day, look for a gray fisher's sweater and a partly rubbed-away embroidered initial. Ellen has a heart-shaped face and prominent ears, with a long plait tucked inside the collar. Ellen presses the lips together to keep a smile in during a conversation.","personality":"Ellen enjoys bargaining, including over things already settled. It is partly a joke and partly a test of whether the other person feels able to say no.","agenda":"To bring something edible to the next railway break.","family":"Jo Emery is Ellen’s cousin raised in the same household. Ellen checks the date twice. Jo brings something that can still be enjoyed tomorrow. Arrangements do change in their family. Taking a delay seriously without treating it as an insult took both of them years. Asked about *The driving lesson fund*, Jo says, “I cannot fund another hour. I offered a place to wait for children whose parents are out with the car.”","connections":"Joanna Ellis. They arrange a lunchtime domino rematch with actual food in the tins.","familyIds":["AH-R1317"],"connectionIds":["AH-R0169"],"reactions":[{"situation":"The night shift misses the collection time","response":"Ellen puts the unclaimed tin by for a later handover.","asWritten":"The night shift misses the collection time. Ellen puts the unclaimed tin by for a later handover."},{"situation":"A traveler asks for the last seat at the bus stop","response":"Ellen gives up their own space if possible and asks the passengers who arrived first to choose what happens next.","asWritten":"A traveler asks for the last seat at the bus stop. Ellen gives up their own space if possible and asks the passengers who arrived first to choose what happens next."},{"situation":"When a friend starts agreeing too quickly","response":"Ellen puts the deal away and suggests a walk.","asWritten":"When a friend starts agreeing too quickly, Ellen puts the deal away and suggests a walk."}]},"appearanceSource":"biography casting design"}},{"mesh":6,"name":"Hair_long01","s